# Theme Development Rules

Active theme: `themes/twintack2025/` (WooCommerce + ACF).

## Conventions

- Use WordPress APIs: `get_template_part()`, `wp_enqueue_script/style`, hooks — no direct file includes for templates
- WooCommerce overrides belong in `themes/twintack2025/woocommerce/` mirroring plugin template paths
- ACF field groups: prefer JSON sync in `acf-json/` when the theme owns field definitions
- Use `home_url()`, `get_template_directory_uri()` — never hardcode `twintack.com`
- Prefix custom functions: `twintack_` or match existing theme prefix

## Asset changes

- Check for existing build pipeline (`package.json`) before editing compiled CSS/JS
- Enqueue in `functions.php` or dedicated inc file — match existing pattern
- Do not add new CSS frameworks unless requested

## When refactoring ported code

1. Preserve behavior first, simplify second
2. Do not delete WooCommerce template overrides without verifying no local override exists
3. Document removed templates in commit message

## Testing checklist

Homepage, shop archive, single product, cart/checkout, custom grip flows, mobile nav.
